<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Point a B3PoW-Scratch miner at <code><%= poolUrl %></code>. Username format is <code>&lt;email&gt;.&lt;workerName&gt;</code>. The password is ignored. Shares are credited when that email matches a registered, verified account.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Reference miner</h2>
  <p>The repo's <a href="https://github.com/b3chain/b3chain/blob/b3chain-main/contrib/miner/b3chain-cpuminer.py">b3chain-cpuminer.py</a> speaks Stratum and checks B3PoW-Scratch shares. It is for connectivity checks, not production hashrate.</p>
  <pre>python3 b3chain-cpuminer.py \
  --stratum <%= poolUrl %> \
  --user you@example.com.rig1 --pass x</pre>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Difficulty</h2>
  <p>Starting difficulty is <strong><%= defaultDifficulty %></strong>.
  <% if (vardiffEnabled) { %>
    Variable difficulty is on. The pool retunes each connection toward one share about every <strong><%= vardiffTargetSeconds %></strong> seconds.
  <% } else { %>
    Variable difficulty is off. Connections stay at the starting difficulty.
  <% } %>
  </p>
  <p>The pool checks each share with B3PoW-Scratch, the same proof the node uses for a block. A share that also meets the network target is submitted as a block.</p>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
